      "writtenOn": "2015-04-30T21:49:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "motion_sense_suspend actually accesses the sensors over the i2c bus and writes some registers to save power in S3 *if* the sensors are initialized. This is OK in other boards where the sensors stay powered in S3. For cyan/strago this is not OK because sensors loose power. So I mark them \"not initialized\" as soon as S3 transition occurs.",
      "parentUuid": "70f8f2fa_ad88dfba",
      "revId": "13a1fd807b1508cee31957c1ce5c858470c130c0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70f8f2fa_b6882cbb",
        "filename": "board/strago/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 157,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-04-30T22:08:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So basically, you are marking them uninitialized here in order to skip the generic cleanup in motion_sense_suspend, right? That\u0027s why you needed to choose a priority higher than MOTION_SENSE_HOOK_PRIO.\n\nAnother question -- why is +V3p3S gated by PCH signal SLP_S3# and not instead by a signal that the EC can assert?",
      "parentUuid": "b017cafa_c4e9c8b2",
      "revId": "13a1fd807b1508cee31957c1ce5c858470c130c0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
